# Commit Message Format Rule (Cursor)

This rule defines the format for all commit messages in the repository.

## Requirements

- Name: "Commit Message Format"
- Pattern: \.git/COMMIT_EDITMSG$
- Description: "Follow the 50/72 rule for commit messages with specific required sections"
- Severity: Warning

## Format Rules

1. The first line should be a concise summary of 50 characters or less
2. The second line should be blank
3. The main body should wrap at 72 characters
4. The body must include the following sections:
   - **Changes added:** Brief description of what was added or changed
   - **Problem:** Description of the issue being addressed
   - **Solution:** Explanation of how the changes solve the problem
   - **Testing:** Description of testing performed to verify the changes
     - Include unit test coverage and list added/updated test files
     - Include run commands when relevant (e.g., `npm run test:unit -- i18n.vendor.spec.js`)
   - **Fixes:** Reference to JIRA/NVBug/Issue or other tracking ID (if applicable)

## Additional Guidance

- Prefer conventional commit types (feat, fix, refactor, docs, test, chore, perf, build, ci, style, revert)
- Use a scope when helpful (e.g., i18n, dumps, router, env-locales)
- Use imperative mood in the subject (e.g., "add", "fix", "update")
- If logic changed, unit tests must be added or updated accordingly
- For environment-specific behavior, include the build/serve command used to verify (e.g., `npm run build -- --mode nvidia-gb`)

## Examples

Subject (≤50 chars): feat(i18n): add vendor overlay fallback

Changes added:
- Merge `src/env/locales/<env>` with vendor-root fallback; auto-discover base locales

Problem:
- Base locales contained vendor-specific strings; overlays needed for multiple NVIDIA projects

Solution:
- Load all base locales dynamically; merge vendor overlays from shared `nvidia/` and variant folders

Testing:
- Added/updated unit tests: tests/unit/i18n.vendor.spec.js
- Run: `npm run test:unit -- i18n.vendor.spec.js`
- Build verification: `npm run build -- --mode nvidia-gb`

Fixes:
fixes nvbug https://nvbugspro.nvidia.com/bug/12345

## Checklist (include at end of body)

- [ ] Linted and formatted
- [ ] Unit tests added/updated and passing (`npm run test:unit`)
- [ ] Build verified for active env (`npm run build -- --mode <env>`)
- [ ] No vendor-specific strings in base locales